-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  str_print_float_spec.adam - print / println / FormatStr write a float32 /
  float64 with a spec as std::format does (M3.8f5; truth
  tests\probe\adam_fmt\fmt_float_oracle.pcpp): e E f F g G a A, a precision
  written or from an argument (6 for e f g without one; no type with one is
  general), ties to even on the exact value (decimal and hex), carries into a
  new digit, general's switch to scientific, `#` (a point always, g's zeros),
  sign, fill / align / width, `0` after the sign (never for inf / nan), inf /
  nan of either sign upper case for A E F G, zeros of either sign, the least
  denormal and the greatest finite, precisions past the digits a float has
  (trailing zeros), float32 forms.
*******************************************************************************/

